  * addresses a memory device by page number, so a misaligned array would
  * shift every read by the offset inside the page.
  *
- * /sbin/launchd is a 4 KB file, not the 2 KB it used to be: before parsing a
- * Mach-O the kernel reads round_page(sizeof(mach_header) + sizeofcmds) bytes
- * of load commands into the kernel, and a short read there is reported as
- * LOAD_BADMACHO.  The image now fills the whole device.
+ * /sbin/launchd has to be a whole kernel page (16 KB): this board has more
+ * than 1 GB of RAM, so arm64 runs with PAGE_SHIFT_CONST = 14 and the kernel
+ * reads round_page(sizeof(mach_header) + sizeofcmds) = 16384 bytes of load
+ * commands before it parses anything.  A shorter file makes that read short
+ * and the kernel answers LOAD_BADMACHO (which killed the first exec).
+ * The device is 20 KB: the table, /etc/hostname, /etc/motd and launchd.
  */
